  "report": "Long-question rows now show both yes/no buttons, and short rows look the same as before. I confirmed this on the iPhone 17 simulator, but I haven't committed anything.\n\n## What I changed\nOne line in `src/components/QuestionRow.tsx`:\n\n```diff\n-  question: { fontSize: 15 },\n+  question: { fontSize: 15, flexShrink: 1 },\n```\n\n**Cause:** the question text could not shrink, so a long title took up the whole row width and pushed the yes/no buttons off the right edge. `flexShrink: 1` lets the text wrap and leaves room for the buttons. I used it instead of `flex: 1` because `flex: 1` would also move the buttons to the right edge on every short row.\n\n## What I checked\n- **Before the fix:** the two long Cleaning questions had no yes/no buttons on screen or in the accessibility tree. These were \"Are the customer toilets cleaned…\" and \"Is the area behind the bakery ovens…\".\n- **After the fix (hot-reloaded through Metro):**\n  - Both long rows wrap to 4 and 3 lines, with yes/no at the right edge.\n  - Short rows (\"Floors clean\", \"Bins emptied\", the red \"!\" rows) have identical positions before and after.\n  - Tapping \"yes\" on a long row highlighted it and changed the header to \"1 of 48 answered\".\n  - I scrolled through every section (Safety through Security) and every question row had both buttons.\n\n## A separate bug I didn't fix\nAfter I answered the toilets question, \"Name badges worn\" in the Staff section showed \"yes\" highlighted though I never tapped it. The header still said \"1 of 48 answered\", so only the display is wrong. This looks like the list reusing row components while `QuestionRow` keeps its own `useState(item.answer)`, which never resets when a row is reused for a different question.\n\nI'm inferring that from the code, not from a test. It doesn't depend on this layout change. It could mislead an auditor, so it deserves its own ticket."
